 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "72 is Paradise: `light` mood (no garden), no river, gold or dwelling drawn; only a light motif for «ورضوان من الله أكبر». 71: light for the prayer and for «سيرحمهم الله», coins for the zakat. STAGING v4: c1 (71): a prayer hall by day; three believers (the believing men and women of the verse are shown by a believers group; no woman is drawn as a figure). They pray on 71:11 and bow on 71:12 (establishing the prayer), facing the empty side of the hall (nobody stands there while they pray); then they stand up on 71:13 and give the zakat on 71:14 to a poor man who sits on the right (he appears only on 71:14, after they have stood up from the prayer, so nobody bows toward him; the zakat is a real obligatory charity, and the poor are its first category in 9:60); he raises his hands on 71:15. Nothing is acted for enjoining good and forbidding evil (a speech toward the empty side is avoided). A geometric plate from 71:19 (His mercy, Mighty and Wise). c2 (72) stays ambient (Paradise): no garden, river, gold or dwelling drawn; the plate on 72:17 (His good pleasure) is now geometric instead of light (a light plate must not start on His attribute). The cover now shows the believers in prayer (71:12)."
